"every 2 seconds (the ``repeat``). Use:"
msgstr "将启动一个重复定时器：``timeout`` 为 5 秒，也就是 ``uv_timer_start`` 执行 5 秒后首次触发，然后每 2 秒（即 ``repeat``）重复一次。使用："

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:33
msgid ""
"to stop the timer. This can be used safely from within the callback as "
"well."
msgstr "来停止定时器。在回调内部使用它也是安全的。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:35
msgid "The repeat interval can be modified at any time with::"
msgstr "重复间隔可以随时通过以下方式修改："

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:39
msgid ""
"which will take effect **when possible**. If this function is called from"
" a timer callback, it means:"
msgstr "修改会 **在可能时** 生效。如果此函数是在定时器回调中被调用的，则意味着："

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:42
msgid ""
"If the timer was non-repeating, the timer has already been stopped. Use "
"``uv_timer_start`` again."
msgstr "如果定时器原本不是重复定时器，那么它已经被停止了。请再次调用 ``uv_timer_start``。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:44
msgid ""
"If the timer is repeating, the next timeout has already been scheduled, "
"so the old repeat interval will be used once more before the timer "
"switches to the new interval."
msgstr "如果定时器是重复定时器，下一次超时已经被调度，因此在定时器切换到新间隔之前，旧的重复间隔还会再被使用一次。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:48
msgid "The utility function::"
msgstr "以下实用函数："

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:52
msgid ""
"applies **only to repeating timers** and is equivalent to stopping the "
"timer and then starting it with both initial ``timeout`` and ``repeat`` "
"set to the old ``repeat`` value. If the timer hasn't been started it "
"fails (error code ``UV_EINVAL``) and returns -1."
msgstr "仅适用于 **重复定时器**，它等价于先停止定时器，然后再以初始 ``timeout`` 和 ``repeat`` 都设为旧 ``repeat`` 值的方式启动它。如果定时器尚未启动，该函数会失败（错误码 ``UV_EINVAL``）并返回 -1。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:57
msgid ""
"An actual timer example is in the :ref:`reference count section "
"<reference-count>`."
msgstr "实际的定时器示例见 :ref:`reference count section <reference-count>`。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:63
msgid "Event loop reference count"
msgstr "事件循环引用计数"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:65
msgid ""
"The event loop only runs as long as there are active handles. This system"
" works by having every handle increase the reference count of the event "
"loop when it is started and decreasing the reference count when stopped. "
"It is also possible to manually change the reference count of handles "
"using::"
msgstr "只要还有活动的句柄，事件循环就会一直运行。这一机制的原理是：每个句柄在启动时增加事件循环的引用计数，停止时减少引用计数。也可以通过以下方式手动更改句柄的引用计数："

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:73
msgid ""
"These functions can be used to allow a loop to exit even when a watcher "
"is active or to use custom objects to keep the loop alive."
msgstr "这些函数可用于让循环在监视器仍处于活动状态时也能退出，或者用自定义对象来保持循环存活。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:76
msgid ""
"The latter can be used with interval timers. You might have a garbage "
"collector which runs every X seconds, or your network service might send "
"a heartbeat to others periodically, but you don't want to have to stop "
"them along all clean exit paths or error scenarios. Or you want the "
"program to exit when all your other watchers are done. In that case just "
"unref the timer immediately after creation so that if it is the only "
"watcher running then ``uv_run`` will still exit."
msgstr "后者可用于周期定时器。你可能有一个每隔 X 秒运行一次的垃圾回收器，或者你的网络服务会周期性地向其他方发送心跳，但你不想在所有正常退出路径或错误场景中都得先把它们停掉。或者你希望程序在所有其他监视器都结束后退出。在这种情况下，只需在创建定时器后立即对其执行 unref，这样即使它是唯一仍在运行的监视器，``uv_run`` 也依然会退出。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:84
msgid ""
"This is also used in node.js where some libuv methods are being bubbled "
"up to the JS API. A ``uv_handle_t`` (the superclass of all watchers) is "
"created per JS object and can be ref/unrefed."
msgstr "node.js 中也使用了这一机制，libuv 的一些方法借此被提升到 JS API。每个 JS 对象都会创建一个 ``uv_handle_t`` （所有监视器的超类），并可以对其进行 ref/unref。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:88
msgid "ref-timer/main.c"
msgstr "ref-timer/main.c"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:95
msgid ""
"We initialize the garbage collector timer, then immediately ``unref`` it."
" Observe how after 9 seconds, when the fake job is done, the program "
"automatically exits, even though the garbage collector is still running."
msgstr "我们初始化垃圾回收器定时器，然后立即 ``unref`` 它。观察一下 9 秒后模拟任务完成时程序是如何自动退出的，尽管那时垃圾回收器仍在运行。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:100
msgid "Idler pattern"
msgstr "Idler 模式"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:102
msgid ""
"The callbacks of idle handles are invoked once per event loop. The idle "
"callback can be used to perform some very low priority activity. For "
"example, you could dispatch a summary of the daily application "
"performance to the developers for analysis during periods of idleness, or"
" use the application's CPU time to perform SETI calculations :) An idle "
"watcher is also useful in a GUI application. Say you are using an event "
"loop for a file download. If the TCP socket is still being established "
"and no other events are present your event loop will pause (**block**), "
"which means your progress bar will freeze and the user will face an "
"unresponsive application. In such a case queue up and idle watcher to "
"keep the UI operational."
msgstr "idle 句柄的回调在每个事件循环中都会被调用一次。idle 回调可用于执行一些优先级极低的活动。例如，你可以在空闲期间向开发者分发一份应用程序当日性能摘要供其分析，或者利用应用程序的 CPU 时间来进行 SETI 计算 :) 在 GUI 应用程序中，idle 监视器也很有用。假设你正在用一个事件循环进行文件下载。如果 TCP 套接字仍在建立中，又没有其他事件，你的事件循环就会暂停（**阻塞**），这意味着进度条会冻结，用户将面对一个无响应的应用程序。在这种情况下，可以排入一个 idle 监视器来保持 UI 正常运作。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:113 ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:126
msgid "idle-compute/main.c"
msgstr "idle-compute/main.c"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:120
msgid ""
"Here we initialize the idle watcher and queue it up along with the actual"
" events we are interested in. ``crunch_away`` will now be called "
"repeatedly until the user types something and presses Return. Then it "
"will be interrupted for a brief amount as the loop deals with the input "
"data, after which it will keep calling the idle callback again."
msgstr "这里我们初始化 idle 监视器，并将它与我们所真正感兴趣的事件一起排入队列。此后 ``crunch_away`` 会被反复调用，直到用户输入一些内容并按下回车键。然后，在循环处理输入数据的那一小段时间里它会被中断，之后循环又会继续不断调用 idle 回调。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:135
msgid "Passing data to worker thread"
msgstr "向工作线程传递数据"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:137
msgid ""
"When using ``uv_queue_work`` you'll usually need to pass complex data "
"through to the worker thread. The solution is to use a ``struct`` and set"
" ``uv_work_t.data`` to point to it. A slight variation is to have the "
"``uv_work_t`` itself as the first member of this struct (called a baton "
"[#]_). This allows cleaning up the work request and all the data in one "
"free call."
msgstr "使用 ``uv_queue_work`` 时，通常需要把复杂的数据传递给工作线程。解决办法是使用一个 ``struct``，并把 ``uv_work_t.data`` 设置为指向它。一个小的变体做法是让 ``uv_work_t`` 本身作为该 struct 的第一个成员（称为 baton [#]_）。这样可以只通过一次 free 调用就清理掉工作请求和所有数据。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:167
msgid "Here we create the baton and queue the task."
msgstr "这里我们创建 baton 并将任务排入队列。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:169
msgid "Now the task function can extract the data it needs:"
msgstr "现在任务函数就可以提取它所需的数据："

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:189
msgid "We then free the baton which also frees the watcher."
msgstr "然后我们释放 baton，这也同时释放了监视器。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:192
msgid "External I/O with polling"
msgstr "利用轮询进行外部 I/O"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:194
msgid ""
"Usually third-party libraries will handle their own I/O, and keep track "
"of their sockets and other files internally. In this case it isn't "
"possible to use the standard stream I/O operations, but the library can "
"still be integrated into the libuv event loop. All that is required is "
"that the library allow you to access the underlying file descriptors and "
"provide functions that process tasks in small increments as decided by "
"your application. Some libraries though will not allow such access, "
"providing only a standard blocking function which will perform the entire"
" I/O transaction and only then return. It is unwise to use these in the "
"event loop thread, use the :ref:`threadpool` instead. Of course, this "
"will also mean losing granular control on the library."
msgstr "第三方库通常自行处理 I/O，并在内部管理自己的套接字和其他文件。在这种情况下，无法使用标准的流 I/O 操作，但仍然可以把该库集成到 libuv 事件循环中。所需的只是：该库允许你访问底层的文件描述符，并提供按你的应用程序的决定以小步增量处理任务的函数。不过，有些库不允许这样的访问，只提供一个标准的阻塞函数，它会执行完整的 I/O 事务然后才返回。在事件循环线程中使用这类函数是不明智的，应改用 :ref:`threadpool`。当然，这也意味着失去对该库的细粒度控制。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:205
msgid ""
"The ``uv_poll`` section of libuv simply watches file descriptors using "
"the operating system notification mechanism. In some sense, all the I/O "
"operations that libuv implements itself are also backed by ``uv_poll`` "
"like code. Whenever the OS notices a change of state in file descriptors "
"being polled, libuv will invoke the associated callback."
msgstr "libuv 的 ``uv_poll`` 部分就是利用操作系统的通知机制来监视文件描述符。从某种意义上说，libuv 自身实现的所有 I/O 操作背后也都有类似 ``uv_poll`` 的代码支撑。每当操作系统注意到被轮询的文件描述符发生状态变化，libuv 就会调用相应的回调。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:211
msgid ""
"Here we will walk through a simple download manager that will use "
"libcurl_ to download files. Rather than give all control to libcurl, "
"we'll instead be using the libuv event loop, and use the non-blocking, "
"async multi_ interface to progress with the download whenever libuv "
"notifies of I/O readiness."
msgstr "这里我们将逐步讲解一个简单的下载管理器，它使用 libcurl_ 来下载文件。我们不会把全部控制权都交给 libcurl，而是使用 libuv 事件循环，并利用非阻塞、异步的 multi_ 接口，在 libuv 通知 I/O 就绪时推进下载。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:219
msgid "uvwget/main.c - The setup"
msgstr "uvwget/main.c - 初始设置"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:226
msgid ""
"The way each library is integrated with libuv will vary. In the case of "
"libcurl, we can register two callbacks. The socket callback "
"``handle_socket`` is invoked whenever the state of a socket changes and "
"we have to start polling it. ``start_timeout`` is called by libcurl to "
"notify us of the next timeout interval, after which we should drive "
"libcurl forward regardless of I/O status. This is so that libcurl can "
"handle errors or do whatever else is required to get the download moving."
msgstr "每个库与 libuv 集成的方式各不相同。就 libcurl 而言，我们可以注册两个回调。套接字回调 ``handle_socket`` 会在套接字状态发生变化、需要开始对其轮询时被调用。``start_timeout`` 由 libcurl 调用，用于通知我们下一个超时时间间隔，在此之后无论 I/O 状态如何，我们都应当驱动 libcurl 向前推进。这样 libcurl 才能处理错误，或者执行让下载继续推进所需的其他操作。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:234
msgid "Our downloader is to be invoked as::"
msgstr "我们的下载器按如下方式调用："

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:238
msgid "So we add each argument as a URL"
msgstr "因此我们把每个参数都作为一个 URL 加入"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:240
msgid "uvwget/main.c - Adding urls"
msgstr "uvwget/main.c - 添加 URL"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:247
msgid ""
"We let libcurl directly write the data to a file, but much more is "
"possible if you so desire."
msgstr "我们让 libcurl 直接把数据写入文件，但如果你愿意，还可以做得更多。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:250
msgid ""
"``start_timeout`` will be called immediately the first time by libcurl, "
"so things are set in motion. This simply starts a libuv `timer "
"<#timers>`_ which drives ``curl_multi_socket_action`` with "
"``CURL_SOCKET_TIMEOUT`` whenever it times out. "
"``curl_multi_socket_action`` is what drives libcurl, and what we call "
"whenever sockets change state. But before we go into that, we need to "
"poll on sockets whenever ``handle_socket`` is called."
msgstr "libcurl 会在第一次立即调用 ``start_timeout``，于是整个流程开始运转。它只是启动一个 libuv `timer <#timers>`_，每当定时器超时，就驱动一次 ``curl_multi_socket_action`` 并传入 ``CURL_SOCKET_TIMEOUT``。``curl_multi_socket_action`` 是驱动 libcurl 的函数，也是我们在套接字状态变化时调用的函数。但在深入讨论之前，我们需要在 ``handle_socket`` 被调用时对套接字进行轮询。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:257
msgid "uvwget/main.c - Setting up polling"
msgstr "uvwget/main.c - 设置轮询"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:264
msgid ""
"We are interested in the socket fd ``s``, and the ``action``. For every "
"socket we create a ``uv_poll_t`` handle if it doesn't exist, and "
"associate it with the socket using ``curl_multi_assign``. This way "
"``socketp`` points to it whenever the callback is invoked."
msgstr "我们关心的是套接字 fd ``s`` 和 ``action``。对每个套接字，如果相应的 ``uv_poll_t`` 句柄还不存在，我们就创建一个，并用 ``curl_multi_assign`` 把它与该套接字关联起来。这样，无论何时回调被调用，``socketp`` 都指向它。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:269
msgid ""
"In the case that the download is done or fails, libcurl requests removal "
"of the poll. So we stop and free the poll handle."
msgstr "当下载完成或失败时，libcurl 会请求移除轮询。因此我们停止并释放 poll 句柄。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:272
msgid ""
"Depending on what events libcurl wishes to watch for, we start polling "
"with ``UV_READABLE`` or ``UV_WRITABLE``. Now libuv will invoke the poll "
"callback whenever the socket is ready for reading or writing. Calling "
"``uv_poll_start`` multiple times on the same handle is acceptable, it "
"will just update the events mask with the new value. ``curl_perform`` is "
"the crux of this program."
msgstr "根据 libcurl 希望监视哪些事件，我们以 ``UV_READABLE`` 或 ``UV_WRITABLE`` 开始轮询。此后，只要套接字可读或可写，libuv 就会调用 poll 回调。在同一个句柄上多次调用 ``uv_poll_start`` 是可以接受的，它只会用新值更新事件掩码。``curl_perform`` 是这个程序的核心。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:278
msgid "uvwget/main.c - Driving libcurl."
msgstr "uvwget/main.c - 驱动 libcurl。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:285
msgid ""
"The first thing we do is to stop the timer, since there has been some "
"progress in the interval. Then depending on what event triggered the "
"callback, we set the correct flags. Then we call "
"``curl_multi_socket_action`` with the socket that progressed and the "
"flags informing about what events happened. At this point libcurl does "
"all of its internal tasks in small increments, and will attempt to return"
" as fast as possible, which is exactly what an evented program wants in "
"its main thread. libcurl keeps queueing messages into its own queue about"
" transfer progress. In our case we are only interested in transfers that "
"are completed. So we extract these messages, and clean up handles whose "
"transfers are done."
msgstr "我们做的第一件事是停止定时器，因为在这段间隔内已经有了一些进展。然后，根据触发回调的事件，我们设置正确的标志。接着，我们用发生进展的套接字以及告知发生了哪些事件的标志来调用 ``curl_multi_socket_action``。此时，libcurl 会以小步增量完成它的所有内部任务，并尽可能快地返回，这正是事件驱动程序在主线程中所希望的。libcurl 会不断把有关传输进度的消息排入它自己的队列。在我们的例子中，我们只关心已完成的传输。因此我们提取这些消息，并清理传输已完成的句柄。"

#: ../../src/guide/utilities.rst:296
msgid "uvwget/main.c - Reading transfer status."
msgstr "uvwget/main.c - 读取传输状态。"

